.\" man/man3/Docv::CrystalPages::Pages.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::CrystalPages::Pages" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::CrystalPages::Pages \- Builds every page of a shard: the overview and one page per documented type.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::CrystalPages::Pages\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Builds every page of a shard: the overview and one page per documented
type.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBIMPLICIT_SUPERCLASSES = {"Reference", "Struct"}\fR
Superclasses every class or struct has, left out of declarations.
.TP 4
\fBMEMBER_SECTIONS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
MEMBER_SECTIONS = { {"CONSTRUCTORS", "def self.", \->(type : TypeDoc) do
  type.constructors
end}, {"CLASS METHODS", "def self.", \->(type : TypeDoc) do
  type.class_methods
end}, {"INSTANCE METHODS", "def ", \->(type : TypeDoc) do
  type.instance_methods
end}, {"MACROS", "macro ", \->(type : TypeDoc) do
  type.macros
end} }
.EE
.RE
.PP
Member sections in page order: title, declaration keyword, members.
.RE
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.new(shard : Shard, types : Types, output : String)\fR
\fIoutput\fR is the output directory as it appears in each page\(aqs path
comment.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef all : Array(Page)\fR
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/crystal_pages/pages.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
